---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { FACULTY, EDGES, inquiryLink } from '../../data/program';

const title = 'Who We Are: The Enterprise Edge';
const description =
  'Bruce Scheer, Dean Edwards and Sandy Yu. One who sells value, one who approved the deals, one who grows the account. Each leads one hour of The Enterprise Edge.';
const canonical = 'https://getenterpriseedge.com/faculty/';

/* Initials for the monogram fallback, so a person without a headshot still
   gets a portrait-shaped element and the row does not collapse to text. */
const initials = (name) =>
  name.split(/\s+/).map((w) => w[0]).join('').slice(0, 2).toUpperCase();

const slugFor = (edgeName) => EDGES.find((e) => e.name === edgeName)?.slug;
---
<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical}>

  <section class="band band-ink hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Who we are</p>
      <h1>Three people. Three sides of the same deal.</h1>
      <p class="lede">We came at enterprise revenue from different chairs, and we kept arriving at the same conclusion about where it goes wrong.</p>

      <div class="pull">
        <p><b>Bruce</b> will get your customers to say yes. <b>Dean</b> will make sure the damn deal closes. <b>Sandy</b> will help you grow the account.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {FACULTY.map((p, i) => (
    <section class={`band ${i % 2 === 0 ? 'band-bone' : 'band-bone2'}`}>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="person">
          <div class="person-photo">
            {p.photo
              ? <img src={p.photo} alt={p.name} width="220" height="220" loading="lazy" />
              : <span class="mono" aria-hidden="true">{initials(p.name)}</span>}
          </div>
          <div class="person-text">
            <p class="eyebrow">
              <a href={`/${slugFor(p.edge)}/`}>{p.edge}</a>
            </p>
            <h2>{p.name}</h2>
            {p.title && <p class="person-title">{p.title}</p>}
            <p set:html={p.bio} />
            {p.awards && (
              <div class="creds">
                <p class="creds-label">Awards and recognition</p>
                <ul>
                  {p.awards.map((a) => <li>{a}</li>)}
                </ul>
              </div>
            )}
            <p class="person-cta">
              <a class="btn" href={inquiryLink(p)}>Email {p.name.split(' ')[0]}</a>
              <a class="more" href={`tel:${p.phone}`}>{p.phoneDisplay}</a>
              {p.site && (
                <a class="more" href={p.site} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{p.siteLabel}</a>
              )}
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}

  <section class="band band-ink band-measure">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Three practices. One point of view.</h2>
      <p>We arrived at the same problem from three different directions and found we were describing one motion, not three. Acquisition that does not survive approval is not revenue. Approval that does not lead to growth is a single transaction. Growth without a story the customer believes is a renewal you have to win twice.</p>
      <p>We built this so a revenue leader hears the whole arc in one morning, from the three of us together, instead of assembling it from three vendors over three years.</p>
      <div class="cta-pair">
        <a class="btn" href="/#dates">See dates and cities</a>
        <a class="more" href="/work-with-us/">Bring the program in-house</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
